=======================================================================
Prior art
=======================================================================

The projects below shaped Mallow's design through their ideas,
behaviours, file formats and public documentation.

NO CODE from any of these projects is included in Mallow's 0BSD
frontend (MallowKit, the mallow command-line tool, the Mallow app, and
the repository scripts). Every line of the frontend is written fresh.
Where a type name or a behaviour matches one of these projects, the
implementation is our own.

Some of these projects (Wine, DXMT, DXVK-macOS, MoltenVK) will also be
distributed by Mallow as separate components, unmodified or built from
their published source, under their own licences. Those components are
not part of the 0BSD frontend. See THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.


Wine
  https://www.winehq.org/
  The compatibility layer that everything in Mallow is built on.
  Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later. The Mallow Runtime will be a build of
  Wine, downloaded separately from the app, under Wine's licence, with
  its complete corresponding source.

CodeWeavers' LGPL Wine sources
  https://www.codeweavers.com/crossover/source
  CodeWeavers publishes the Wine sources behind its products under the
  LGPL, and funds a large share of Wine development, especially on
  macOS. The Mallow Runtime will be built from that source release.
  Mallow uses only those LGPL sources, under their licence, and never
  any proprietary CodeWeavers file.

Whisky
  https://github.com/Whisky-App/Whisky  (GPL-3.0, archived)
  Showed what a simple, native SwiftUI Wine frontend for Apple Silicon
  can look like.

frankea/Whisky
  https://github.com/frankea/Whisky  (GPL-3.0)
  A maintained Whisky fork. Ideas: importing Apple's Game Porting
  Toolkit from the user's own copy, choosing a graphics backend with a
  resolver, the "hide D3D12" preset, per-program NVAPI rules, and its
  Steam compatibility notes. Some Mallow type names match its names
  (WineEnvironment, DLLOverrides, GPTKImporter, BottleSettings).
  Also frankea/winecx-gptk (https://github.com/frankea/winecx-gptk),
  whose build notes and Steam findings were read for ideas only.

Heroic Games Launcher
  https://github.com/Heroic-Games-Launcher/HeroicGamesLauncher  (GPL-3.0)
  How a game launcher builds the Wine environment for each game.

Bottles
  https://github.com/bottlesdevs/Bottles  (GPL-3.0)
  The bottle configuration model, and writing configuration files
  atomically (write a temporary file, then rename it).

Mythic
  https://github.com/MythicApp/Mythic  (GPL-3.0)
  Downloading and updating Wine engines from a catalog.

Gcenx's Wine builds
  https://github.com/Gcenx/macOS_Wine_builds
  https://github.com/Gcenx/macports-wine
  WineHQ packages for macOS, which Mallow plans to offer as an interim
  "Standard Wine" runtime, and the WINEDLLPATH_PREPEND idea: a private
  DLL search path that lets graphics backends take priority over Wine's
  own DLLs. Mallow's runtime patch uses the same variable name for
  compatibility, but it is our own implementation.

DXMT
  https://github.com/3Shain/dxmt
  Direct3D 10 and 11 translation to Metal. To be distributed by Mallow
  as a separate graphics backend under its own licence (MIT up to
  v0.80, LGPL-2.1-or-later afterwards).

DXVK-macOS
  https://github.com/Gcenx/DXVK-macOS
  The macOS build of DXVK (https://github.com/doitsujin/dxvk), which
  translates Direct3D to Vulkan. To be distributed by Mallow as a
  separate graphics backend under its own licence (zlib).

MoltenVK
  https://github.com/KhronosGroup/MoltenVK
  Vulkan on top of Metal. To be included in the Mallow Runtime under
  its own licence (Apache-2.0).

Also consulted, for ideas and facts only:
  - winetricks (https://github.com/Winetricks/winetricks, LGPL-2.1-or-later).
    Download URLs and hashes are facts and may appear in Mallow's CC0
    recipes; script logic is never copied. Mallow will download
    winetricks itself, unmodified, when a user first needs it.
  - wine-msync (https://github.com/marzent/wine-msync).
  - highball-engine (https://github.com/gauthierpiarrette/highball-engine),
    for its pinned build inputs and CI experience.


